{{Infobox/WorkbenchPlugin
|name= Doxygen Filler
|editor= script
|descr= Create/Format Doxygen documentation skeleton for configured methods (default public methods only)
|file= {{Link|enfusion://ScriptEditor/scripts/WorkbenchGame/ScriptEditor/SCR_DoxygenFillerPlugin.c}}
|shortcut= {{Controls|Ctrl|Alt|Shift|D}}
}}

'''Doxygen Filler''' is a plugin that automatically adds a [[Doxygen]] skeleton structure to document methods properly, e.g:
<enforce>
//!
//! \param[in] entity
//! \param[out] health
//! \return
bool IsSoldierAlive(notnull IEntity entity, out float health = 0)
{
	// ...
}
</enforce>


== Parameters ==

* '''Doxygen public/protected/private methods''': tick to add a Doxygen skeleton to public/protected/private methods respectively {{Feature|informative|It is considered good practice to at least document the public API.}}
* '''Doxygen overridden/static/obsolete methods''':
** documenting overridden methods is not always wanted, unless the override drastically changes the method's behaviour
** documenting static methods is also a good practice, see public/protected/private methods above
** documenting obsolete methods may not be worth it, depending on the context
* '''Partial Doxygen Prefixes''': method prefixes for which no description field is added (e.g {{hl|'''Get'''Health()}}, self-explanatory enough); if emptied, refilled with {{hl|Get}}, {{hl|Set}}, {{hl|On}}, {{hl|Is}}
* '''Convert Doxygen Formatting''': converts comment blocks <enforce inline>/*! */</enforce> into inline comments <enforce inline>//!</enforce>, preferred <table style="min-width: 75em"><tr><td style="width: 50%"><enforce>
/*!
This is a comment
Made in one block
Try not to use this format too much,
As it sometimes conflicts with other comments
*/
</enforce></td><td><enforce>
//!
//! This is a comment
//! Made in one block
//! Try not to use this format too much,
//! As it sometimes conflicts with other comments
//!
</enforce></td></tr></table>Note that top/bottom lines can be removed here.
* '''Add Missing Separators''': add the infamous method separator on methods not having it<br><enforce inline>//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</enforce>
* '''Add Constructor Normal Comment''': add a simple <enforce inline>// constructor</enforce> comment, helpful in case of class renaming and forgetting to rename the constructor
* '''Add Destructor Normal Comment''': same with <enforce inline>// destructor</enforce>, so the constructor would not feel singled out


