==== Code Comments ====
Code comments are surprisingly '''not''' a must-have for inside code; code organisation combined to variable names should be enough to be read by a human, '''then''' comment can be used:
* a comment should explain '''''why''''' the code is written this way
* a comment should not tell '''''what''''' the code does; code should be self-explanatory
* as a last resort in the event of a complex piece of code, a comment can be used to describe what the code actually does - or at least its intention

On the other hand, ''documentation'' is more than welcome as it provides information from the outside without having to read the code. Enfusion uses {{Link|Doxygen}}.

==== Files Organisation ====
{{Feature|informative|See {{Link|Arma Reforger:Directory Structure}} to know how/where to organise script files (Scripts\GameCode).}}

* Have one class/enum per file
** Small classes/enums can always be grouped together in the same file, provided they are part of the same system or only used there
* Use (sub-)directories to group related classes together


{{GameCategory|armaR|Modding|Scripting|Guidelines}}

{{TOC|side}}
{{Feature|informative|
Format reminder:
* '''camelCase''' is writing by gluing words together and making their first letter capital, but for the first one, e.g {{hl|namingLikeThis}}.
* '''PascalCase''' is writing in '''camelCase''' but with the first letter set uppercase, e.g {{hl|NamingLikeThis}}.
* '''snake casing''' ({{hl|naming_like_this}}) is '''not''' a convention used in Enfusion.<br>Only {{hl|const}} values should be {{hl|NAMED_LIKE_THIS}}.
}}


== Tag ==

To prevent conflict with other scripts all classes, and global functions must be distinguished by a [[Scripting Tags|Tag]].

{{Name|bi}} scripts have been prefixed with {{hl|SCR_}}. A mod developer must choose their own tag and not use one already taken by {{Name|bi}} or another developer.

When {{Link|Arma Reforger:Scripting Modding|modding}} any class, all methods and variables within that modded class must also be distinguished by the same unique tag to prevent conflict.


== File/Class ==

* File should be called {{hl|TAG_MyObject.c}}
** A component must end with "component": {{hl|TAG_ExampleComponent.c}}
** An entity must end with "entity': {{hl|TAG_ExampleEntity.c}}
* Class should be called the same (without file extension):
** {{hl|class TAG_MyObject}}
** {{hl|class TAG_ExampleComponent}}
** {{hl|class TAG_ExampleEntity}}
* Enum:
** name must be prefixed with a capital E, e.g {{hl|TAG_EMyEnum}}
** values use all capital letters with words separated by underscores, e.g {{hl|TAG_EMyEnum.VALUE_1}}
* The file should be located in the {{hl|scripts\Game}} directory
* The use of plural is prohibited at the end of combined keywords: e.g {{hl|TAG_Notification'''s'''Component}} &rarr; {{hl|TAG_NotificationComponent}}


== Method ==

* '''Functions'''/'''Methods''' naming uses '''PascalCase''', e.g:<enforce>int ReturnNumber()</enforce>
* Parameters are named with '''camelCase''', e.g:<enforce>int ReturnNumber(bool canBeNegative)</enforce>


